---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { PROFILE } from '../data/profile';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Corrections policy"
  description="How to report a factual error, broken reference, outdated API note, or accessibility problem at ORIZ.IN, and what happens next."
  lastUpdated="25 October 2026"
>
  <p>
    ORIZ.IN aims to be accurate, but it is maintained by one person. Errors
    happen. Corrections are welcome and are handled as editorial work, not as
    customer-support tickets.
  </p>

  <h2>What to report</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>a factual or mathematical error;</li>
    <li>a broken internal link or an external source that has moved;</li>
    <li>an API endpoint, CORS behavior, rate limit, or authentication detail that has changed;</li>
    <li>a tool result that contradicts its documented behavior;</li>
    <li>an accessibility barrier or keyboard trap;</li>
    <li>a licensing, attribution, or copyright concern.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to report it</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${PROFILE.email}?subject=Correction`}>{PROFILE.email}</a>
    with the subject “Correction”. Include:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>the page URL;</li>
    <li>the exact sentence, example, or result that is wrong;</li>
    <li>why it is wrong;</li>
    <li>a primary source or a reproducible test, where one applies.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Reproducible tool bugs can also be filed in the
    {' '}
    <a href="https://github.com/chirag127/oriz.in/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer">public issue tracker</a>.
    Do not include passwords, personal data, or private production details in a
    public issue.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens next</h2>
  <p>
    Reports are reviewed against the source and the current site behavior. When
    a correction is warranted, the page is updated and its “last updated” date
    is revised where the page displays one. Significant corrections may be
    described in the updated text; there is currently no separate public
    corrections log.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is no guaranteed response time. Corrections are prioritised by
    severity: a dangerous financial or security error first, then broken
    references and factual errors, then minor copy edits.
  </p>

  <h2>What this policy is not</h2>
  <p>
    A correction request is not a way to remove accurate criticism, an
    unfavourable reference entry, or an opinion clearly labelled as such. If you
    disagree with an interpretation, send the reasoning and a source; the
    response may be a clarification rather than a deletion.
  </p>

  <h2>Security reports</h2>
  <p>
    For a vulnerability, email {PROFILE.email} with the subject “Security” and
    enough detail to reproduce the issue. Please do not test against other
    visitors, exfiltrate data, or cause disruption. This is a small static site;
    there is no bug bounty program.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Related policies: <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>,
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy</a>, and <a href="/contact/">contact</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
